uropean and 1999 World Championship, and was favored. But in her heat, she collided with another runner, fell, and was out of the competition. Without her, the final was wide open. The first lap of the final was absurdly slow, at over 70 seconds, the lead taken by " [:a {:href "/athletes/89163"} "Marla Runyan"] " (USA), who was partially blind. America’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/77822"} "Suzy Favor-Hamilton"] " then took over and led for most of the next two laps, fighting off several challenges. Going into the final turn, she still led with Romania’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/75096"} "Violeta Szekely"] " and Algeria’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/64272"} "Noria Mérah-Benida"] " on her shoulder. Mérah-Benida took the lead coming into the final straight and would not be caught, although Szekely pushed her to the end, finishing only 0.05 down. Romania’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/75153"} "Gabriela Szabo"] " had been almost in last place on the backstretch but closed strongly to get the bronze medal."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "1024"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/64272"} "Nouria Mérah-Benida"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/ALG"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/ALG.png"}] "ALG"]] [:td {} "4:10.24 (2 h3)"] [:td {} "4:05.24 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "4:05.10 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "2833"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/75096"} "Violeta Szekely"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/ROU"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/ROU.png"}] "ROU"]] [:td {} "4:10.18 (1 h2)"] [:td {}